## 8. Oracle Monitor Service

### 8.1 Monitor Architecture

```go
// retropick-oracle: polls each configured Chainlink feed every 60 seconds
// Writes to oracle_health table
// Emits alerts via keeper_alert NOTIFY channel and alert service

type OracleMonitor struct {
    feeds    map[string]FeedConfig   // feedId → {adapter, heartbeatSec}
    pgConn   *pgxpool.Pool
    client   *ethclient.Client
    alerter  AlertDispatcher
}

type FeedConfig struct {
    FeedID        []byte
    AdapterClass  string
    AdapterAddr   string
    HeartbeatSec  int       // Chainlink's advertised heartbeat
    MaxDelaySec   int       // from template oracle config
    Label         string    // "BTC/USD", "ETH Staking APR"
}

// Check logic per feed:
// 1. Read latestRoundData() from Chainlink proxy
// 2. Compute staleness: now - updatedAt
// 3. If staleness > maxDelaySec * 0.8: WARN alert (20% buffer before keeper fails)
// 4. If staleness > maxDelaySec: CRITICAL alert + open incident
// 5. If roundId went backwards: CRITICAL alert (oracle regression)
// 6. Write to oracle_readings and oracle_health
```

