---
title: Getting started
---

New to RetroPick? Start with **What you need**, then **Wallets & network** if you will connect a wallet.

You do not need to understand smart contracts to use the product—these pages focus on what to expect in the app.
</file>

<file path="apps/docs/contents/docs/getting-started/wallets-and-network.mdx">
---
title: Wallets & network
---

## For non-crypto readers

Think of a wallet as your **account** for on-chain markets: it holds the keys that prove you own positions and can withdraw winnings. RetroPick does not “log you in” with a password alone—you connect a wallet the same way many DeFi apps do.

## Connecting a wallet

1. Install a supported wallet (browser extension or mobile).
2. Open the RetroPick app and choose **Connect**.
3. Confirm the connection request in your wallet.

## Network

Make sure your wallet is on the **same network** the app expects (e.g. a testnet or mainnet deployment). If the network is wrong, transactions will fail or go to the wrong chain.

## Approvals and gas

When you trade with ERC-20 tokens, you may need to **approve** the protocol contract to move a limited amount of your tokens. Each transaction consumes **gas** paid in the chain’s native asset.

### Technical note

Use block explorers to verify contract addresses and transactions. Never share **seed phrases** or **private keys** with anyone or any website.
</file>

<file path="apps/docs/contents/docs/getting-started/what-you-need.mdx">
---
title: What you need
---

## Everyone

- A **clear question** on each market: what is being measured, and when does the round end?
- Read the **resolution rules** on the market page before you put money in.
- Understand you can **lose your stake** if your side does not win (except in a **void**, where rules may return deposits).

## Crypto essentials (short)

- A **wallet** app that supports the chain RetroPick runs on for your deployment.
- **Stablecoins** (often USDC) are commonly used to enter pools—subject to what the app supports.
- Small amounts of the chain’s **native token** pay **transaction fees (gas)** when you approve, deposit, claim, etc.

### Technical note

Exact tokens, chains, and UI flows can change by deployment. Follow the in-app prompts and the official RetroPick interfaces only.
</file>

